35,2,1,talk,Misaki,,"It turns out that weekly repeating trips are often the ones that collapse, and the car is sometimes left dirty or with almost no fuel. This explains why it's so unreliable on a plain morning.","{""words"":35,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
36,2,1,talk,May,,"It's even worse than I thought. Recording every run took nearly an hour a week! Plus, the diary shows we use the car way more on Saturdays and during holidays than on Tuesdays. The coordination is a nightmare.","{""words"":38,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
37,2,1,talk,Servas,,"My findings reveal that our fixed costs are quite significant, exceeding 280,000 yen annually. More concerningly, I've learned that attempting to audit one another's figures created a climate of accusation and apology.","{""words"":32,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
38,2,1,talk,Takumi,,"That's exactly what I feared. Other groups said that asking for favors or clinging to turns ruins things. Plus, checking each other's figures just makes us feel accused. We can't have a system that feels like policing.","{""words"":37,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
39,2,1,talk,Kenji,,"Wow, the fuel receipts are totally lopsided! Two people paid for most of it, and one person barely paid anything. Also, we use the car way more on Saturdays and holidays than on weekdays!","{""words"":34,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
40,2,2,talk,Misaki,,"@Kenji, the lopsided fuel costs and the state of the car are linked. If some people aren't paying, they might not be taking responsibility for refueling or cleaning it for the next person.","{""words"":33,""mentions"":[""Kenji""],""raw_differs"":false}"
41,2,2,talk,May,,"@Misaki, exactly. And if we try to fix that by recording every single trip, we're just adding another hour of work a week to our plates. We need a system that's automatic, not a second job.","{""words"":36,""mentions"":[""Misaki""],""raw_differs"":false}"
42,2,2,talk,Servas,,"It seems we are caught between the need for precision and the risk of resentment. If auditing our figures breeds accusation, perhaps we should seek a structure that minimizes the need for such scrutiny.","{""words"":34,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
43,2,2,talk,Takumi,,"@Servas, I totally agree. If checking figures makes us fight, we should stop doing it. We need a way to share the car where we don't have to ask for favors or feel like we're being watched.","{""words"":37,""mentions"":[""Servas""],""raw_differs"":false}"
44,2,2,talk,Kenji,,But we can't just ignore the fuel! It's not fair that only two people are paying for almost everything. We need a way to make the payments even without making everyone feel accused.,"{""words"":33,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
45,2,3,talk,Misaki,,"If we want to avoid the ""policing"" Takumi mentioned, we can't rely on manual recording. We need a system where the responsibility for the car's state and fuel is clear and automatic.","{""words"":32,""mentions"":[""Takumi""],""raw_differs"":false}"
46,2,3,talk,May,,"I agree. If we spend an hour a week just tracking numbers, we're just replacing one headache with another. We need something that doesn't require us to be accountants or secretaries just to go for a drive.","{""words"":37,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
47,2,3,talk,Servas,,"It is a delicate balance. We must ensure that no one is unfairly burdened, yet we must avoid the bitterness that comes from constant surveillance. Perhaps a system of fixed responsibility is the path to peace.","{""words"":36,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
48,2,3,talk,Takumi,,"@Servas, that sounds right. If we have fixed roles or days, we don't have to ask for favors every time, which is what other groups said ruins the mood. It keeps things simple and friendly.","{""words"":35,""mentions"":[""Servas""],""raw_differs"":false}"
49,2,3,talk,Kenji,,"I get that, but we still need to fix the money part! If we just have fixed days, how do we make sure the person who barely paid for fuel finally chips in? We need a fair way to pay!","{""words"":40,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
50,2,4,talk,Misaki,,"@Kenji, if we have a fixed monthly share, the payment is automatic. We won't have to track every single liter of fuel or argue over who paid last, which solves the fairness issue without the policing.","{""words"":36,""mentions"":[""Kenji""],""raw_differs"":false}"
51,2,4,talk,May,,"That sounds perfect. If we have a fixed share and set days, we stop the endless coordinating and the tedious recording. It saves us time and keeps the peace. I'm all for something simple.","{""words"":34,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
52,2,4,talk,Servas,,"It seems we have found a common thread. By removing the need for constant auditing and negotiation, we protect our friendship while ensuring the car's burdens are shared. Simplicity is often the greatest kindness we can show one another.","{""words"":39,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
53,2,4,talk,Takumi,,"I'm with you all. If we stop the constant asking and checking, we stop the fighting. Let's go for the simplest option that keeps us from acting like police officers.","{""words"":30,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
54,2,4,talk,Kenji,,"I guess you're right. If a fixed share means everyone pays their fair part without us having to fight over receipts, then I'm in! Let's pick the simplest way to make it fair.","{""words"":33,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
