60,3,1,talk,Misaki,,"Given our findings, Option A seems best. It solves the issue of repeating trips collapsing and removes the need for the tedious recording and auditing that causes friction. It's the most stable and automatic choice.","{""words"":35,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
61,3,1,talk,May,,I completely agree with Misaki. Option A eliminates the hour of weekly recording and the constant coordinating. It's the only choice that gives us our free time back while keeping the payments simple and fair.,"{""words"":35,""mentions"":[""Misaki""],""raw_differs"":false}"
62,3,1,talk,Servas,,"Option A aligns with the wisdom of simplicity. By establishing a fixed structure, we remove the seeds of resentment and the burden of surveillance, allowing our shared journey to be one of peace rather than accounting.","{""words"":36,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
63,3,1,talk,Takumi,,I'm voting for Option A. It stops us from having to ask for favors and avoids the policing that makes us grumpy. It's the best way to keep our friendship strong and the car easy to use.,"{""words"":37,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
64,3,1,talk,Kenji,,"I'm voting for Option A too! It makes the money fair with the fixed share, and we don't have to fight over receipts. Let's go with the simplest plan and keep being friends!","{""words"":33,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
